NAME
       strtol, strtoul, strtod, atoi - convert a string to a number

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdlib.h>

       long          strtol(const char *s, char **end, int base);
       unsigned long strtoul(const char *s, char **end, int base);
       double        strtod(const char *s, char **end);
       int           atoi(const char *s);

DESCRIPTION
       Parses a number from the front of S, skipping leading
       whitespace and accepting a leading + or -. With base 0 a 0x
       prefix means hexadecimal and a leading 0 means octal. END, when
       not NULL, is set to the first unparsed character.

       atoi is strtol with base 10 and no error reporting.

RETURN VALUE
       The value, or 0 when nothing could be parsed.

SEE ALSO
       printf(3), expr(1)
